/-!
# A finite bound for the exact max2 presentation

The subgroup generated by the seven fixed words is an image of the checked
presentation of order at most 3840. The 693-coset cover of the original
presentation then gives 3840 * 693 = 2661120. Both finiteness and the cardinal
bound follow from the certificates; no GAP order or model identification is
assumed. The 29 original relators keep ordinary multiplication order.

Source motivation: GLS3 Table 5.3i, printed p.270. The fixed witnesses and
their untrusted discovery are documented in `FiniteBound/source/README.md`.
-/

namespace Janko4.OuterReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.TwoCoreCentralizerData.NormalClosureControl.ActionKernel.Presentation

/-- The actual group on the 29 published relators is finite and has at most
2,661,120 elements. -/
public theorem presentation_finite_card_le : Finite Group ∧ Nat.card Group ≤ 2661120 := by
  exact FiniteBound.finite_card_le_of_child FiniteBound.level1Relator
    FiniteBound.level0Generator FiniteBound.liftedRelations01
    FiniteBound.stabilizer_finite_card_le FiniteBound.Cover0.cover

end Janko4.OuterReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.TwoCoreCentralizerData.NormalClosureControl.ActionKernel.Presentation
